# A missing hashed asset must 404 rather than fall through to the SPA rule.
# Serving index.html (200 text/html) for a deleted chunk makes dynamic imports
# fail with a parse error and lets a caching service worker store HTML under a
# .js URL, which bricks the app until its cache is cleared. Netlify serves any
# asset that actually exists BEFORE consulting redirects, so this only catches
# genuinely-missing files. The :splat destination is required — Netlify ignores
# a rule with a bare status and no target. Must stay above /* — first match wins.
# Kept in sync with netlify.toml, which declares the same pair.
/assets/*    /assets/:splat    404
/*    /index.html   200
